      "descriptionHtml": "<p><b>No needles. Just real acupressure.</b> This auto-sensing acupressure pen locates pressure points and delivers gentle electronic stimulation at the push of a button — the same meridian-point technique used in traditional acupuncture, without the needles, the training, or the appointment.</p>\n\n<h3>Why people are switching to this over traditional tools</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<b>Auto point-sensing</b> — the tip detects acupoints automatically, so you don't need to know pressure-point charts to use it correctly</li>\n<li>\n<b>Multiple head styles</b> — choose 3-head or 5-head tips, oil-free or oil-infused, depending on sensitivity and use case</li>\n<li>\n<b>Durable build</b> — ABS + aluminum alloy body designed for daily use</li>\n<li>\n<b>Portable</b> — compact enough for a desk drawer, gym bag, or carry-on</li>\n<li>\n<b>Multi-purpose</b> — home massage, post-workout recovery, everyday tension relief</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Who it's for</h3>\n<p>Anyone dealing with everyday muscle tension, stress, or stiffness who wants a faster, needle-free alternative to traditional acupuncture — at home, on your schedule.</p>\n\n<h3>FAQ</h3>\n<p><b>Is this the same as acupuncture?</b><br>It uses the same meridian/pressure-point principle as acupuncture, but stimulates points electronically instead of with needles.</p>\n<p><b>Do I need training to use it?</b><br>No — the auto-sensing tip is designed to find active points without prior knowledge of acupoint charts.</p>\n<p><b>Is it safe for daily use?</b><br>Yes, it's designed for regular home use. As with any massage tool, avoid use directly over broken skin, varicose veins, or if pregnant without consulting a doctor.</p>\n<p><b>What's the difference between the head styles?</b><br>3-head tips are more precise for smaller areas; 5-head tips cover broader muscle groups faster. Oil-infused variants glide more smoothly on skin.</p>\n\n<p><i>This is a wellness/massage tool, not a medical device. Individual results vary.</i></p>",
